# sheep-and-fire.speak — the first program written in Ninia speak.
# The hybrid: a burning fire, sheep that flee it, wolves that hunt.
# Every sentence lowers to compiled machinery in the nina runtime.

-- CONFIG --
GRID IS 33 BY 33
WORLD IS 2.0 WIDE
TIME FROM 0 TO 12 BY 0.1
SEED IS 11

-- DATA --
temperature IS FIELD
alpha IS NUMBER WITH VALUE 0.05
fire IS SPOT AT 0.25, 0.25
sheep IS SPECIES WITH energy
wolves IS SPECIES WITH energy

-- VERBS --
DEFINE VERB graze AS
    WANDER $
    GROW energy OF $ BY 0.02
END VERB

-- SETUP --
MAKE 40 sheep AT RANDOM WITH energy 1.5
MAKE 4 wolves AT RANDOM WITH energy 1.5
SOLVE dtemperature/dt = alpha * lap(temperature) + temperature * (1 - temperature)
APPLY BOUNDARY zero TO temperature
HOLD temperature AT 5.0 WITHIN 0.25 OF fire

-- SIMULATION --
STEP THE FIELD
FOR EACH s IN sheep DO
    MOVE s AWAY FROM GRADIENT OF temperature
    MOVE s AWAY FROM wolves WITHIN 0.08
    GRAZE s
    SPLIT s WHEN energy ABOVE 2.5
REPEAT
FOR EACH w IN wolves DO
    HUNT w EATING sheep WITHIN 0.06 GAINING 1.5
    GROW energy OF w BY -0.03
    WANDER w
REPEAT
REAP sheep BELOW 0.0
REAP wolves BELOW 0.0
REPORT COUNT OF sheep AND COUNT OF wolves AND MEAN temperature AND temperature AT sheep EVERY 20
